# ==== T-FMT-C · `on error` — suite-layout form preservation
#
# AXIS (2 cells): inline (COLON-LESS) · block.
#
# ⚠ THE INLINE FORM TAKES NO COLON. `on error print(1)` parses;
#   `on error: print(1)` is a PARSE ERROR (measured 2026-08-11 —
#   `expected NEWLINE, found identifier 'print'`). So this site's inline
#   header suffix differs from every other suite in the family, which is why
#   the inline emitter takes the header spelling as a per-site parameter
#   rather than hardcoding `":"`.
#
# RED pre-fix (recorded 2026-08-11): the inline cell EXPLODED to
#   `on error:` + an indented body — three hunks on the S1 corpus sweep.
# GREEN pre-fix / BREAK-AND-WATCH: the block cell; make the emitter ignore
#   `Block.layout` (always inline) and it collapses onto the header.

void inline_form():
    on error print(1)
    print(2)

void block_form():
    on error:
        print(1)
        print(3)
    print(2)

void main():
    inline_form()
    block_form()
